    {
      "id": "where-i-am-how",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "How to read this",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 340
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 360,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Where am I?\n\n**186 graphs** across your library and canon: 78 task graphs, 18 plans, 36 ideas, 40 smoke tests, demos and Q&A. It was written from the graphs themselves (a task graph's goal status and task counts, and when the file last changed in git) on 2026-10-25, so it can be run again. **37 task graphs are in the archive** (`tasks/archive/2026/q3`) and are left out of the lists below.\n\n**The sort.** *Now* = changed since 2026-10-19. *Started, then quiet* = some tasks done or in progress, nothing touched since. *Not started* = every task still to do. *Finished* = the goal is done. *Cancelled* = the goal is cancelled. \"yours\" is your personal library; \"canon\" is the Twilite Zone repository.\n\n**One fact about the dates.** Almost everything older than 2026-10-19 was last changed on 15 October, in one burst: the Methods, events, Bridges and workspace work. So \"quiet\" mostly means \"since that burst\", not \"abandoned\"."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-now",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Now",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 740
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 860,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Now (18)\n\nWhat has moved since 2026-10-19.\n\n- **Authoring switches** (yours plans/authoring-switches, 2026-10-25)\n- **Carry Class Events Across Bridges** (yours tasks/bridge-class-scoped-events, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 5 todo, 1 open question\n- **Events: Occurrence and Delivery Contract** (yours tasks/events-occurrence-delivery, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 5 done, 3 in-progress, 1 todo\n- **Method calls leave a trace** (yours tasks/method-traceability, 2026-10-25) — todo: 5 todo, 2 open questions\n- **Michael's Task Collection** (yours tasks/root, 2026-10-25): 1 in-progress, 1 waiting, 1 todo\n- **Move Event Subscriptions onto Bridges** (yours tasks/bridge-owned-event-subscriptions, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 6 done, 3 in-progress\n- **Move Failure Policy to the Handler** (yours tasks/handler-method-failure-policy, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 5 todo, 1 open question\n- **Primitives, self-documenting** (yours tasks/primitives-self-documenting, 2026-10-25) — in-progress: 4 done, 1 waiting, 4 todo, 1 cancelled\n- **Reuse One Method From Two Handlers** (yours tasks/method-reuse-two-handlers, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 5 todo, 1 open question\n- **Show Events in the Bridge Editor** (yours tasks/bridge-editor-events, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 2 done, 2 in-progress, 1 todo\n- **Smoke Test Export and Import** (yours tasks/bridge-events-smoke, 2026-10-25) — cancelled: 5 todo, 1 open question\n- **The Properties panel and the authoring contract** (yours tasks/properties-and-authoring-contract, 2026-10-25) — in-progress: 4 done, 2 waiting, 9 todo, 5 open questions\n- **Where am I?** (yours plans/where-i-am, 2026-10-25)\n- **Expandable Graph Rooms** (yours ideas/expandable-graph-rooms, 2026-10-23)\n- **Graph Standardization** (yours ideas/graph-standardization, 2026-10-23)\n- **Canon templates in order** (yours tasks/canon-templates-in-order, 2026-10-22) — in-progress: 5 done, 7 todo, 2 open questions\n- **A workspace bar that says what it does** (yours plans/workspace-toolbar, 2026-10-20)\n- **Twilite Zone graphs follow the view-shape rule** (yours tasks/canon-view-shape-consistency, 2026-10-20) — in-progress: 1 done, 1 blocked, 3 todo, 1 open question\n\n**Not in this list because they have no root graph of their own:** the handle demos (`plans/handles-demo`), the new primitive drafts (`plans/new-primitives`: environment, ground, event), and the task for the work in front of you, `tasks/properties-and-authoring-contract`."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-quiet",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Started, then quiet",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1640
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 590,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Started, then quiet (11)\n\nSome of the work is done or under way, and nothing has changed since 2026-10-19. These are the ones most likely to be nearly finished, or quietly overtaken by other work.\n\n- **Unify workspace and graph space** (yours tasks/workspace-graph-space-unification, 2026-10-18) — in-progress: 4 done, 3 in-progress\n- **Validate workspace graph saving and connection dragging** (yours tasks/workspace-save-connection-validation, 2026-10-18) — in-progress: 2 in-progress\n- **Beta Readiness** (canon tasks/beta-readiness, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 6 done, 5 in-progress, 2 todo\n- **Declaration Surfaces: Make the Spec True** (canon tasks/declaration-surfaces, 2026-10-15) — open: 6 done, 5 in-progress, 1 todo\n- **Give Bridges Role-Shaped Sections** (yours tasks/bridge-editor-sections, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 4 in-progress, 1 todo, 1 open question\n- **Implement Edge Endpoint Reassignment** (yours tasks/edge-endpoint-reassignment, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 2 in-progress, 5 todo\n- **Implement Graph-Authored Ports and Handles** (yours tasks/ports-and-handles-interface, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 5 done, 2 in-progress, 1 todo\n- **New User Experience** (canon tasks/new-user-experience, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 1 in-progress, 1 open question\n- **Property Nodes and Inline Editing** (yours tasks/property-node-inline-editor, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 3 done, 6 in-progress\n- **Template Video and UI Polish** (yours tasks/template-video-ui-polish, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 7 done, 2 in-progress, 1 open question\n- **Workspace Graph-Node Projection** (canon tasks/workspace-graph-node-projection, 2026-10-15) — in-progress: 9 in-progress, 3 todo, 1 open question"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-audit",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Started, then quiet: audited",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2270
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 1490,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Started, then quiet: audited\n\nFrom reading each task graph's goal and tasks and checking them against the code and its tests. I did not run the app for each one, so \"done\" below means the code and tests say so, not that I watched it work.\n\n**Done on 25 October.** Group A is closed and archived (the goal given its status and the reason, a portal in `tasks/archive/2026/q3`). In group D, `zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model` and `ui-analysis` are cancelled and archived, and `wikipedia-browser-template-design` and `chat-node-provenance` are parked (goal waiting) and archived. Each graph in group B has a line on its goal saying where its remainder went. C is untouched.\n\n## A. Done in fact: close and archive (9)\n\n- **Page stacked view assembly** (yours). Every task is done: the Page Template's Method builds the stacked view, and `pageMethodSync` tests hold it. Two open questions were answered by building it.\n- **Page front door from pieces** (yours). The public root is now built from the Public Arrival template and the Page Template; this was the experiment that led there.\n- **Resource resolution and web content** (yours). The resolver and its tests exist (`nodeResolvers`, `representationResolver`). Two tasks are left: validating navigation end to end, which needs a browser run, and Twilite-hosted tlz retrieval, which twilite.zone now provides.\n- **Continuous view resolution** (canon). `semanticZoom.resolution` is built and in the face editor. Left: \"migrate compatibility and verify visual behavior\".\n- **Edge classes** (canon, August). `library/edges` holds the classes and `edgeLegality` enforces them. The open question, how much behavior belongs on an edge class, was answered by building it.\n- **Workspace bridge apertures** (canon). Written as a reversible experiment. The geometry is built and used (`ownerAperture`, `targetAperture` in `workspaceBridge.js` and `workspaceCapabilities.js`), so the experiment concluded.\n- **Focus-sized workspace** (canon). `focusTransition` and `workspaceFocusByScale` are built and tested. Its free-mode tasks no longer apply: the free version has no workspace.\n- **Revised save workflow** and **Semantic zoom** (canon). Each is a single done task with no goal.\n\n## B. Mostly built: the rest belongs to a newer task (6)\n\n- **Ports and handles interface** (yours). The contract, compiler, dispatch and geometry are done, and this week finished the drawing and dragging. What is left (the Port configuration UI, migrating the root) is the handles editor in `properties-and-authoring-contract`.\n- **Graph organization law** (canon). Five of six done. The last, \"make useful graph forms recognizable and reusable\", is what `canon-templates-in-order` does.\n- **Workspace graph-space unification** (yours). Four done; drag and hit testing now work (checked this week), and \"persistence and browser regression proof\" cannot be had, because the repo has no browser test runner.\n- **Workspace graph-node projection** (canon). This is the border-handle and drop work of the last few days. Open: endpoint drops as relationship operations, end-to-end validation, migrating defaults. Most of its \"in progress\" is probably done.\n- **Edge endpoint reassignment** (yours). `reconnectEdge` is in `GraphCrud.js` and the reconnect session is in `HandleLayer.js`, so the core is built. Open: the smoke graph and endpoint selectors in the edge editor.\n- **Property node inline editor** (yours). The class, `propertyState` and four tests exist. Most tasks say in progress; the in-app check is what is missing.\n\n## C. Still real (4)\n\n- **Beta readiness** (canon). The launch list.\n- **New user experience** (canon). One task, one open question.\n- **Workspace save and connection validation** (yours). Two drafts about the save transaction; nothing since.\n- **Declaration surfaces** (canon). A progress note from 24 September: tasks 1 to 6 built, 7 not started. It still says \"Declaration\" where the model now says root. Needs rewriting in today's words or folding into the authoring contract task.\n\n## D. Stale, park or decide (6)\n\n- **Zoom level: floor from content, ceiling from allotted space** (yours). No text, four tasks to do; overtaken by continuous view resolution. Cancel.\n- **UI analysis** (canon, May). Twenty-three tasks with no titles, five months old. Archive.\n- **Wikipedia browser template design** (yours). A design for one specimen. Park as an idea.\n- **Chat node provenance** (yours). A prototype; there is no chat node class in canon. Park.\n- **Template video and UI polish** (yours). A demo-video task with eight untitled tasks. Yours to decide.\n- **Bridge editor sections** (yours). Its first task is obsolete and its subject is real: `BridgeSetupEditorSection.js` exists, and grants still appear in the Properties panel, so \"move them out\" is not done. Keep, with the obsolete task removed.\n\n## What I would do\n\nClose A and archive D's stale ones the way the event graphs were done: goal marked, reason written, a portal in the archive. For B, put one line on each saying where its remainder went. Leave C alone. That closes 13 and leaves 12: the six in B, the four in C, and the two in D that wait on you (the demo video, and Bridge editor sections)."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
