    {
      "id": "where-i-am-ideas",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Ideas and plans",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5560
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 1850,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Ideas (34) and plans (14)\n\nAll last changed on or before 15 October, none of them task graphs. Nothing here is \"to do\"; these are the thinking the task graphs came from.\n\n**Plans**\n\n- Canon at twilite.zone (yours plans/canon-at-twilite-zone)\n- Canon or Personal (yours plans/canon-or-personal)\n- Direct Edge Routing and Route Pins (yours plans/direct-edge-routing)\n- Electron Desktop Conversion (yours plans/electron-desktop-conversion)\n- Events run Methods through edges (yours plans/events-through-edges)\n- Fragment Extraction Authoring Contract (yours plans/fragment-extraction-authoring-contract)\n- Methods Through the Bridge (yours plans/methods-through-the-bridge)\n- One Bridge per Template (yours plans/one-bridge-per-template)\n- Operation Northwoods Research Plan (yours plans/operation-northwoods)\n- Primitive Template Collection (yours plans/primitive-template-collection)\n- Public Root: Welcome, Learn More, Explore (yours plans/public-root-arrival)\n- Reciprocal Multi-Graph Bridge Contract (yours plans/reciprocal-multigraph-bridge-contract)\n- Twilite’s vocabulary, in layers (yours plans/vocabulary)\n- What’s next (yours plans/whats-next)\n\n**Ideas**\n\n- A Solid Method Node (yours ideas/method-node-design)\n- Active Fragment Authoring Scope (yours ideas/active-fragment-authoring-scope)\n- Chat Nodes as Graph Provenance (yours ideas/chat-node-provenance)\n- Edge Endpoint Reassignment (yours ideas/edge-endpoint-reassignment)\n- Focus as a First-Class Presentation Context (yours ideas/focus-model)\n- Graph-Native Chemistry (yours ideas/graph-native-chemistry)\n- Graph-Owned Capabilities (yours ideas/graph-owned-capabilities)\n- Idea Template (yours ideas/edge-and-label-navigation)\n- Installing Templates Into Existing Graphs (yours ideas/installing-templates-into-existing-graphs)\n- MCP Without Losing Copy/Paste (yours ideas/mcp-copy-paste-workflow)\n- Michael's Ideas Collection (yours ideas/root)\n- One Node, Multiple Declarations (yours ideas/multi-declaration-expansion)\n- Ports and Handles as an Authored Interface (yours ideas/ports-and-handles-as-authored-interface)\n- Public Browsing, Paid Production (yours ideas/public-browsing-paid-production)\n- Question-Driven Explanation Template (yours ideas/question-driven-explanation-template)\n- Relationship Handles as Graph Structure (yours ideas/relationship-handles-as-graph-structure)\n- Retune Semantic Zoom Thresholds (yours ideas/retune-semantic-zoom-thresholds)\n- Script Nodes as Placeable Behavior (yours ideas/script-node-presentation)\n- Semantic Zoom as View Selection (yours ideas/semantic-zoom-view-selection)\n- Semantic Zoom Has No Middle Ground (yours ideas/semantic-zoom-architecture)\n- The Bridge Editor (yours ideas/bridge-editor)\n- The Camera Behaves Like the Browser (yours ideas/zoom-and-wheel-behavior)\n- The Page Template (yours ideas/page-template)\n- The Stroke Control (yours ideas/stroke-control)\n- Twilite Front Door (yours ideas/twilite-front-door)\n- Type and Instance Presentation (yours ideas/type-and-instance-presentation)\n- Typed Inter-Graph Handoff Envelope (yours ideas/typed-inter-graph-handoff-envelope)\n- What an Event Handler Node Should Do (yours ideas/event-handler-behavior)\n- What Could a Node Template Be? (yours ideas/node-template-brainstorm)\n- Wikipedia Article Node (yours ideas/wikipedia-article-node)\n- Windowed Collection Browsing (yours ideas/windowed-collection-browsing)\n- Resource Resolution and Web Content (yours ideas/resource-resolution-and-web-content)\n- Workspace as Recursive Graph Document (canon ideas/recursive-workspace-document)\n- Workspace Semantic Presentation (canon ideas/workspace-semantic-presentation)"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-spare",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Smoke tests, demos and Q&A",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7450
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 1460,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Smoke tests, demos and Q&A (40)\n\nTest fixtures and worked examples. Most were last changed on 14 or 15 October. They are fine to leave, and are the first place to look if something old breaks.\n\n- Class Smoke Test (yours graphs/class-smoketest)\n- Navigation today (yours graphs/navigation-today)\n- Page looks (yours graphs/page-looks)\n- Interaction Arbiter Smoke Test (yours graphs/interaction-arbiter-smoke)\n- Semantic Zoom Fallback Smoke Test (yours graphs/semantic-zoom-fallback-smoke)\n- New graph (yours graphs/fixture-b)\n- New graph (yours graphs/fixture-a)\n- Cross-Graph Interaction and Data Handoff (yours graphs/inter-graph-data-handoff-plan)\n- Example Note Smoke Test (yours graphs/example-note-smoke)\n- Exposed Port Navigation Plan (yours graphs/exposed-port-navigation-plan)\n- Graph Lab (yours graphs/root)\n- How Will Graph-Based Interfaces Change the Web? (yours qa/how-will-graph-based-interfaces-change-the-web)\n- Multiple Installed Workboards Smoke Test (yours graphs/template-installation-multiple-workboards)\n- Script Capability Placement Smoke (yours graphs/script-capability-smoke)\n- Template Installation Smoke Test (yours graphs/template-installation-smoke)\n- Twilite (demo) (yours graphs/twilite-demo)\n- Twilite Is the Matrix (yours graphs/twilite-matrix-browser)\n- Twilite Workspace Persistence (yours qa/workspace-persistence)\n- View Model Simplification Plan (yours graphs/view-model-simplification-plan)\n- What Is Twilite? (yours qa/what-is-twilite)\n- Who Is Twilite For? (yours qa/who-is-twilite-for)\n- Canvas Smoke Test (yours graphs/canvas-smoke-test)\n- Composition Smoke Node (yours graphs/interface-frame-smoke)\n- Declaration Primary View Toolbar Smoke (yours graphs/declaration-primary-view-toolbar-smoke)\n- Edge and Label Navigation Smoke Test (yours graphs/edge-label-navigation-smoke)\n- Episode Structure Map (yours graphs/candace-owens-episode-Ep360)\n- Folder Contents (yours graphs/folder-contents)\n- How Should Focus Work in Twilite? (yours qa/focus-model-spec)\n- Indiana Jones (yours graphs/indiana-jones)\n- Plate Tectonics (yours graphs/plate-tectonics)\n- Primitive Port Layouts (yours qa/primitive-port-layouts)\n- Primitive Port Layouts — Smoke Test (yours qa/primitive-port-layouts-smoke)\n- Q&A Collection (yours qa/root)\n- The Boulevard (demo) (yours graphs/boulevard-demo)\n- The Commons (demo) (yours graphs/commons-demo)\n- The Water Cycle (yours graphs/watercycle)\n- The water cycle (scene demo) (yours graphs/water-cycle-demo)\n- Twilite Front Door Smoke (yours graphs/twilite-front-door-smoke)\n- Twilite: A Graph-Native World (yours graphs/twilite-overview)\n- Wheel and Zoom Test Bench (yours qa/wheel-test-bench)"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-map",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "What this session touched",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8950
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What the recent work touches\n\nThe work of the last few days, and the older graphs it probably belongs to. This is my reading, not something the graphs say, so check each pairing before closing anything.\n\n- **Handles** (drawn on workspace tiles, dragging, the plain 8-ball, art on the border, hover-only signs) → `tasks/ports-and-handles-interface` (yours, in progress) and the canon smoke suite `tasks/graph-defined-handle-smoke-suite`. The first has 5 done, 2 in progress and 1 to do, and has not been updated since. Its tasks may be done now.\n- **Primitive pages, posters, small-tile scaling** → `tasks/canon-templates-in-order` (5 done, 7 to do) and `tasks/canon-view-shape-consistency` (1 blocked), plus the new `tasks/primitives-self-documenting`. Canon's own `tasks/primitive-library` is done.\n- **Authoring switches and the Properties panel** → canon `tasks/authoring-contract-hardening` (open, 4 to do, 2 open questions) is the nearest older plan, and `tasks/property-node-inline-editor` (yours, 6 in progress) is the nearest old work on the editing surface. The new `tasks/properties-and-authoring-contract` is the one to keep; those two may fold into it or close.\n- **Workspace** (tile handles, scope, drag) → `tasks/workspace-graph-space-unification` (3 in progress), `tasks/workspace-save-connection-validation` (2 in progress), and canon `tasks/workspace-graph-node-projection` and `tasks/workspace-bridge-apertures`."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-triage",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "A way to sort it",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9370
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 530,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# A way to sort it\n\nA proposal, to edit.\n\n**Done so far (25 October).** The eight task graphs for the old event design (Handler nodes, Subscriptions, events carried across a Bridge) are marked cancelled with the reason, and the quarter's archive (`tasks/archive/2026/q3`) has a portal to each. Nothing was deleted or moved. The ten finished task graphs that had no place there (three of yours, seven from canon) have a portal in it too, and the finished roadmap is off the active task collection. The one idea from the old event graphs that the code has not done (an id and an outcome for each Method call) is its own small task, `tasks/method-traceability`.\n\n1. **Archive what is finished** (0 task graphs). It costs nothing and takes the list from 78 to 78.\n2. **Close or fold in what the recent work overtook.** Start with the three pairings above: handles, the Properties panel, and canon's `authoring-contract-hardening`.\n3. **Decide the 15 October burst as a set**, not one at a time. It is one program (Methods, events, Bridges, the workspace), 11 task graphs started and 22 not. Either it is a stream you still intend to pick up, in which case it needs a single front-door task graph, or it is background and can be parked.\n4. **Keep three streams open at once, no more.** At the moment these are: *primitives and templates* (canon-templates-in-order, primitives-self-documenting), *the Properties panel and the contract* (the new task graph), and *the workspace* (unification and save validation). Everything else waits.\n5. **Leave the ideas alone.** They cost nothing while they sit.\n\nThe question that decides step 3 is yours: is the Methods, events and Bridges program still the next big thing after the templates, or has the work of the last week replaced it?"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    }
